{"availability":"available","full":"Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness","name":"rag-harness","description":"Reliability-first RAG over Kubernetes docs: grounded, cited, injection-resistant answers with a CI reliability gate, judge audit, and a live streaming demo.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-30T22:01:47Z","updated":"2026-10-05T08:28:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rag-harness-277002385573.us-central1.run.app","topics":["evaluation","fastapi","kubernetes","llm","llm-as-judge","mcp","python","rag","rag-evaluation","reliability"],"demo":"https://rag-harness-277002385573.us-central1.run.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T17:28:02.674Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T17:28:02.674Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T17:28:02.674Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:45:30.285Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:09.323Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:28:02.674Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A reliability lab for retrieval systems, built over the Kubernetes documentation. Most RAG projects stop at a demo. This one treats reliability as the product: it measures answer quality across each failure mode, validates the LLM judge that does the scoring before trusting it, red-teams its own corpus for prompt injection and data poisoning, and gates every change on the numbers with bootstrap confidence intervals. Every claim below links to the ADR and the measured result behind it. The Kubernetes docs are the flagship corpus, but ingestion is corpus-agnostic: point CORPUS at any markdown…","A RAG pipeline has three independent failure modes. Scoring each one independently lets you pinpoint exactly what broke, not just that \"something went wrong\":","The evaluation suite runs against a hand-verified golden set of 160 single-hop cases spanning cluster, networking, rbac, scheduling, storage, and workloads topics, plus dedicated unanswerable (refusal-path) and version-sensitive categories, and an 8-case multi-hop slice (168 reviewed cases in total). The headline quality numbers are on the 160 single-hop cases; the multi-hop slice is scored separately. Thresholds are recalibrated from the ablation to sit below the production config's bootstrap CI lower bounds (see config.py). A build fails when any gated metric drops below its threshold."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f9da3db76a5925fa4ec5331611a2d2b046f5695dedfce9dc99ab7e3c2df05693","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:30.569Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:30.569Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A reliability lab for retrieval systems, built over the Kubernetes documentation. Most RAG projects stop at a demo. This one treats reliability as the product: it measures answer quality across each failure mode, validates the LLM judge that does the scoring before trusting it, red-teams its own corpus for prompt injection and data poisoning, and gates every change on the numbers with bootstrap confidence intervals. Every claim below links to the ADR and the measured result behind it. The Kubernetes docs are the flagship corpus, but ingestion is corpus-agnostic: point CORPUS at any markdown…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no analytics, no other third parties.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Optional API-key auth (APIAUTHENABLED, off","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f9da3db76a5925fa4ec5331611a2d2b046f5695dedfce9dc99ab7e3c2df05693","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Yashbhadiyadra/rag-harness/blob/main/README.md","ch